TELOMERE-CCC2-1:{"chunk":"c01","format":"ccc2-wire/1","records":[{"buys":"The machine is borrowed, but the fuel refines to our face-sum-native weights.","checksum":"30daa71ee81e662cba75ca6b28ec47fb5d59314f1576feef437ca38a062bb7ae","id":"B1","limits":"Exact theorem; the identity is classical — only the USE as a dictionary is ours.","type":"B","x":"CCM's fuel (Λ)","y":"face-sum-native μ, via Λ = μ ∗ log"},{"buys":"The spectral program (13d/13e probes — no prior art).","checksum":"c7a79d0a188edb49a4052382f76c0b50d5270b837188c0565a3fd7149fe9c640","id":"B2","limits":"Independent prior art exists (goldenphysicsproject) — the identification is NOT unique to this work; only the spectral program is ours.","type":"B","x":"Δ_z faces","y":"fermionic Fock basis, μ=(−1)^F"},{"checksum":"26780b7c28ecc68e9f2eab8aa010e4b2ab376de9d35b2f2373cae0ae790c3468","id":"C1","kind":"claim","label":"Node 7 (paper): outline drafted","note":"Awaiting user approval on title/scope + prior-art re-search before public novelty claims. Standing rule: no public novelty claim without re-search; the paper is an expository/synthesis vehicle, not a breakthrough claim.","status":"heuristic","type":"C"},{"checksum":"49c85614f4528bc2a46dd63db7da7874f618d93197c179ecad29bc0fd9b32e74","id":"C2","kind":"claim","label":"Physical build: tetrahedral sieve (z=7) + layered territory wall","note":"Fabrication files not yet created; library time not yet confirmed. [label basis: plan only — fabrication files not yet created, library time not confirmed; heuristic, not established.]","status":"heuristic","type":"C"},{"checksum":"8e3f1fe582d50e9b8aaa55fc0430164943c2bae988a1bbc86f5060a2b5e46939","id":"C3","kind":"definition","label":"D5 — Figueiredo steer (standing methodological decision)","note":"Take her GENERATIVE insights (process), never copy implementation. Territory removal = her 'soft limit/splitting'. Applied throughout.","status":"exact","type":"C"},{"checksum":"f67d68889d0b0a380f00ba8b40419087c83a8de95f04a0ec1c001e7eddb79b21","id":"C4","kind":"definition","label":"Territory/relational reading of the sieve (D2)","note":"n prime ⟺ no shared-boundary relation to earlier prime territory; composites = overlaps of prime territories. The user's relational metaphysics expressed as a machine. Definitional reframing of the sieve rule — proves nothing new about distribution.","status":"exact","type":"C"},{"checksum":"d1189dccea75d051ac76af806a7e66eb5c14a90e27a6c966a6b9a93500cecdd2","id":"C5","kind":"claim","label":"Equivariant Chern-root home for w(S) (14b/14c)","note":"14b IDENTITY (exact): d/du[∏_p(1−p^{−u})]_{u=1}=Σ_S w(S) — face-weights as differentiated residues. 14c REFINED HOME: equivariant Chern roots −u·log p; Figueiredo's deformations supply the mechanism. Closes the D4↔D6 loop. A refined geometric presentation, not a positive region — the positivity gap stands.","status":"exact","type":"C"},{"checksum":"c9eba76b56e48c68e92ffc01289371c297fc4f1ca1cc49f12046c5cb4c64ac5f","generates":[{"prescription":"Build the incidence complex: vertices are primes ≤ x, faces are prime sets co-dividing some integer ≤ x (the nerve of the prime territories).","stage":"complex"},{"prescription":"Form the face-sum with Möbius signs: φ(x,a) = Σ_{d|P_a} μ(d)⌊x/d⌋ — inclusion–exclusion as Euler-characteristic weighting.","stage":"face-sum"},{"prescription":"Read primality off the complex: n prime iff it stands in no shared-boundary relation to earlier prime territory.","stage":"read"}],"honest_boundary":"Classical theorem in new clothes — the math is classical inclusion–exclusion; only the Δ_z framing is claimed new, and that novelty claim rests on a 2026-09-30 prior-art search, not a proof of novelty.","honest_label":"exact","id":"D1","rule":"Sieve = simplicial complex Δ_z (faces = finite prime subsets = squarefree products); φ(x,a) = face-sum Möbius inversion over Δ_x; primality = absence of shared-boundary relation.","subtitle":"Simplicial sieve (Δ_z)","type":"D","verified":[{"check":"reframing consistency","expected":"matches classical inclusion–exclusion counts"}]},{"checksum":"5be72f520ae7aecfb8be833738acf0186b1dc296a812903eab188d7593c55222","generates":[{"prescription":"As x→∞ every finite prime set satisfies ∏S≤x — Δ_∞ is the infinite simplex: contractible, no topology. Geometry must live in the WEIGHTS, not the bare complex.","stage":"bare limit"},{"prescription":"ψ(x)/x = Σ_{∏S≤x} w(S)·(⌊x/∏S⌋/(x/∏S)); the floor cutoff tends to 1.","stage":"weighted sum"},{"prescription":"The Dirichlet GF Σ_S w(S)/∏S^{s−1} = −ζ′(s)/ζ(s)²; the rate of S(X)→1 — the face-sum error — is governed by the zeros of ζ (explicit formula).","stage":"regulators"}],"honest_boundary":"The Σ→1 identity is equivalent to PNT — classical, not proved here; only the 'weighted simplex, total weight 1' statement is claimed new (framing, searched 2026-09-30).","honest_label":"computationally_verified","id":"D3","rule":"w(S)=(−1)^{|S|+1}log(∏S)/∏S; Σ_{∏S≤X} w(S)→1 (X→∞); Dirichlet GF Σ_S w(S)/∏S^{s−1} = −ζ′(s)/ζ(s)².","subtitle":"Weighted infinite complex: PNT as total weight 1","type":"D","verified":[{"check":"Σ w(S) at X=5·10⁵","expected":"0.999922 ≈ 1"},{"check":"GF vs ζ′/ζ² at s=1.01…1.20","expected":"agree to ~4 digits"}]},{"checksum":"6cc7a61166ba4ab52505707cd2a21db7f65ccc94f3f78bcbdc0aceab7b99bf82","generates":[{"prescription":"Deform the marking rule: prime p marks residues R_p={0} (p=2), {0,−2} (p odd) — n marked if p|n or p|(n+2). Markers stay prime; survivors become a new set.","stage":"deform"},{"prescription":"Run the deformed sieve to x=200000 and check survivors against an independent primality sieve.","stage":"identify survivors"},{"prescription":"Renormalize: δ(z)=[∏_{p≤z}(1−1/p)²]·𝔖(z) — the first factor →0 (Mertens); the second converges to 2C₂=1.32032….","stage":"renormalize"}],"honest_boundary":"The algebra is exact, but the passage 𝔖(z)→π₂(x)~𝔖·x/(log x)² is the UNPROVEN twin prime conjecture (ratio 1.6091 at 2·10⁵ vs conjectured 1.3203 — slow convergence); do not present this as progress on the conjecture itself.","honest_label":"exact","id":"D4","rule":"R_p={0}→{0,−2} (p odd); δ(z)=∏_{p≤z}(1−|R_p|/p)=[∏(1−1/p)²]·𝔖(z); 𝔖(z)→2C₂=1.32032….","subtitle":"Deformation → twin constant (generative move)","type":"D","verified":[{"check":"deformed sieve survivors ≤200000","expected":"exactly the 2160 twin prime lowers"},{"check":"𝔖(z) at z=7,13,30,100","expected":"1.367187, 1.344116, 1.330277, 1.322754 → 1.32032"}]},{"checksum":"6d8ac33d85c4539e78b60b2f940d5acac1918f67bcf671bd27b961d6067b3d92","id":"G1","result":"All 32 Fejér–Riesz factors fully dense [computationally verified].","title":"9c′ — saturated degree-16 optimizers","transfer":"Saturation is numerical, not geometric — do not mine optimizers for geometry.","tried":"Saturated degree-16 optimizers, checking for small-support structure.","type":"G","verdict":"No small-support structure — closed negative."},{"checksum":"d609b499fe156d7c9ddd26f63d0a2db31e1db71ed9ca75d0c22ea178c67270cf","id":"G2","result":"Weyl's law kills L1–L3; Heisenberg nilmanifold probe (65,401 eigenvalues) negative on three panels.","title":"12a–12d — multi-torus operator probes","transfer":"Topology alone is insufficient. Surviving form = Deninger's foliated dynamical system — conjectural, formulated not simulated.","tried":"L1–L3 multi-torus Laplacians; Heisenberg nilmanifold probe.","type":"G","verdict":"Laplacians killed; Heisenberg negative."},{"checksum":"00cf5ea5a39b3325d17f00ffc614598901d9eb2fdf55339a7b5423066c0e6620","id":"G3","result":"ξ-invariance verified to 3.77e-16 [exact].","title":"11b — Möbius-band quotient","transfer":"Withdrawn claims stay on the record; the symmetry survives as ξ-invariance.","tried":"s↦1−s̄ symmetry framed as a Möbius quotient.","type":"G","verdict":"CORRECTED — not a Möbius band; claim withdrawn."},{"checksum":"8abc6ccea73e2f03f5bb3a49028287f4e4a52e9c975cf88f305f9e813a1a7608","id":"G4","result":"Computationally verified — topology valid, arithmetic mechanism absent.","title":"11d — Möbius-band Laplacian","transfer":"Topology alone is insufficient for the operator hunt.","tried":"Möbius-band Laplacian as an arithmetic operator candidate.","type":"G","verdict":"Valid topology, no arithmetic mechanism."},{"checksum":"d08e5a27d31434a8e3b2ea34013654c353884bad47b3eabb0efdecaa82eefb20","from":"D1","id":"L1","rel":"depends_on","to":"D3","type":"L"},{"checksum":"e28f791957055e369bd3b25329de41161bfbfbf3ce671f2a967a7ac4c06cf4c2","from":"B1","id":"L2","rel":"supports","to":"V3","type":"L"},{"checksum":"a5d5f17f8299628fb4543917821d50ad208c9fa7600df1f5966ac2a0061d4642","from":"D4","id":"L3","rel":"refines","to":"C5","type":"L"},{"checksum":"54f585071f2e8e085afac43010f19c1e7183fe83f710b94c172917bdbeb49054","from":"V1","id":"L4","rel":"causes","to":"V5","type":"L"},{"checksum":"1049a00dd3d6e980620544fc28cf60637f12354d83a26fafc8996b348b53411e","consequence":"Face-sum carries three verified positivity kinds; none zero-detecting; the missing object is operator-theoretic — this verdict forces the operator hunt (Node 11).","id":"V1","note":"9a: positivity lives in primitive objects (−ζ′/ζ=ΣΛ(n)n^{−s}, Λ≥0; δ(z)>0; 3-4-1) [exact]. 9b: bridge carries traffic — full 3-4-1 as nonnegative stratum energies [computationally verified identity]. 10a: explicit formula grounded in our objects; prime-side zero detector built [computationally verified]. 10b: Li's criterion closed as face-sum-incompatible; Weil's positivity face-sum-native [exact/conceptual]. 10c: EXACT THEOREM — Selberg's λ² form on Δ_z minimized at λ*=μ, minimum δ(z). 10d: function-field template formulated, not simulated. 10e: supporting tools closed (MVT, large sieve, uncertainty wall).","status":"exact","subject":"D7/D9/D10 — positivity located, bridge program complete","type":"V"},{"checksum":"3c6ce5efd64a7fd26965e739c26d7e2781ae6e7f539541eb5ac8aa9fa2dad601","consequence":"Geometry owns positivity, analysis owns continuation; any RH attempt must route around this theorem — positivity cannot be the zero-detector.","id":"V2","note":"'Positivity is blind left of Re(s)=1' — closed negative BY THEOREM, not by failed experiment.","status":"killed","subject":"9c as RH proof","type":"V"},{"checksum":"c9154860868de9fb8d3d6176a922b4399b18ced16e530889b6059548350a0b30","consequence":"CCM is the live operator candidate but fragile — an exact-arithmetic reporter, not a stable gap; small primes dominate; Node 11 stays OPEN pending the full Frobenius-like operator question.","id":"V3","note":"Independent reimplementation from arXiv:2511.22755; zeros 1–8 recovered from primes alone (zero1 exact to float64 at c=13,N=20). Controls: zeros AND positivity require exact prime input (A/B/C all negative). N=120: ε_even=3.48e-59, separation 8771× (monotone 581→3744→8771). Failure modes: drop p=2/3 destroys; drop p=5 survives — fragile, not robust.","status":"computationally_verified","subject":"11f — CCM, the live candidate","type":"V"},{"checksum":"c0338460aa62b9c6fb098a1acfa33dc16e8fbf1410d7fea04d2e0087fe314973","consequence":"The Node 13 fork stays open via 13d (universality result); the bridge-relevant question — an operator that HEARS primes — is unanswered; 13e stays negative.","id":"V4","note":"Exact identification Δ_z faces = fermionic Fock basis, μ=(−1)^F [exact] — BUT independent prior art exists (goldenphysicsproject); the identification is NOT unique to this work. H_2 KILLED BY INSPECTION (integrable). H_int NEGATIVE — Poisson-like bulk. 13d (pair hopping) POSITIVE — GUE-like at all z≥17, all λ; strengthened to z=41 (dim 8192), ⟨r⟩=0.528 [computationally verified]. Caveat: shuffled weights also GUE (generic two-body chaos) — content is arithmetic weights COMPATIBLE with chaos. 13e (prime-frequency probe) NEGATIVE — operator does not HEAR the primes. Our distinct contribution: the spectral program (no prior art); the identification itself is shared.","status":"computationally_verified","subject":"13d/13e — fermionic Fock fork","type":"V"},{"checksum":"2fadd4e6ce92932c0508d0fb1efaf8ca5711a3a946b81fca139bf9938e338578","consequence":"The full Frobenius-like operator question remains open at the conceptual level; the Node 13 fork stays open via 13d (universality); Node 8 stays heuristic, open by nature — the bridge has three verified positivity kinds + one live operator candidate + one exact fuel dictionary.","id":"V5","note":"11a: Berry–Keating xp probe — smooth law captured, fluctuations not [conjectural].","status":"conjectural","subject":"Node 11 — operator hunt (the live frontier)","type":"V"}],"registry":{"B1":"B","B2":"B","C1":"C","C2":"C","C3":"C","C4":"C","C5":"C","D1":"D","D3":"D","D4":"D","G1":"G","G2":"G","G3":"G","G4":"G","L1":"L","L2":"L","L3":"L","L4":"L","V1":"V","V2":"V","V3":"V","V4":"V","V5":"V"},"wire_checksum":"309dde9dd258656f64195f04801df026ba3860531e0557583e93dce2656a81e0"}:TELOMERE-CCC2-1